F009 cohort preparation
======================

This is an unexecuted Source package for later cohorts, after registration
of parents 330..341.  It provides three bounded Root-only metadata entries:

* init_cohort.py checks an explicitly expected registered prefix and freezes
  one new interval of at most twelve parents in batches of at most three.
* issue_phase.py writes a fresh decision and actual bindings, then prints
  the existing adapter command.  It launches no worker.
* close_cohort.py records terminal roles and a zero-or-more metadata retry
  map; a cohort with no retries is supported without a fabricated override.

packet.json and manifest_*.json pin the current literal Source.
PROTOCOL.rst specifies review, Root ownership, fields, CLI arguments,
read/output accounting and the exact boundary with the existing adapter.
legacy_inputs.json and retained/objects contain genuine old bodies needed
by these operations.  Eight unavailable old bookkeeping bodies are listed
as unavailable and are not recreated.  The accepted scientific adapter,
manifests, templates, controls and mathematical premises remain unchanged.

No operational entry, future cohort freeze or canonical write has been
performed.  A distinct Source peer and Root's complete Source/protocol
ownership are required before execution.  The present cohort must first
be registered.  The actual auditor also needs a separately reviewed branch
admitting the new honest V2 metadata Source owner before any future
cohort can pass actual review or be adopted; its existing cohort-330
admission remains unchanged.

The entry manifests charge the complete current entry, common.py, literal
whole.py, both inherited guard bodies and a 512-byte reserve.  Their
totals are 42019 bytes for init, 40780 for phase preparation and 42703
for closing, each below 65536.  Every entry retains 256 MiB/125-second,
64 MiB/512-path and 4 MiB-per-file metadata limits.  Original forest/cache
containers are skipped lexically where only metadata fields are needed.

The existing cohort/decision/summary schemas, scientific paths and SDK
key conventions are preserved.  New control metadata belongs under the
durable cohorts/ directory, which will be created only by a later Root
init.  All exact legacy aliases must match retained whole bytes before
use; the new entries refuse absent or mismatched aliases.
